{"title":"Career Roadmap · Curriculum Developer","role":"Curriculum Developer","summary":"A Curriculum Developer designs, reviews, structures, and improves educational curricula, learning materials, lesson frameworks, assessments, and instructional resources.","facts":{"Current degree":"Other Teacher Education (D.El.Ed / B.El.Ed / B.P.Ed / ITEP / Integrated B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed)","Course":"Integrated Teacher Education (ITEP / B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Curriculum Developer designs, reviews, structures, and improves educational curricula, learning materials, lesson frameworks, assessments, and instructional resources."},{"type":"p","text":"Curriculum Developers can work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Schools and school networks"},{"text":"EdTech companies"},{"text":"Educational publishers"},{"text":"Universities and colleges"},{"text":"Teacher-training organizations"},{"text":"NGOs and education foundations"},{"text":"Government education projects"},{"text":"Assessment organizations"},{"text":"Corporate learning and training companies"},{"text":"Online learning platforms"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["The role combines subject knowledge","pedagogy","instructional design","assessment","educational technology","research."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For an ITEP/B.Sc-B.Ed/BA-B.Ed graduate, Curriculum Developer is usually a career progression rather than an immediate entry-level designation. A strong pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["ITEP / B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed","Teaching Practicum","Teacher / Academic Content Associate","Curriculum / Instructional Design Experience","Curriculum Developer","Senior Curriculum Developer","Curriculum Lead / Academic Lead","Head of Curriculum / Academic Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Stage 1 — Undergraduate"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ITEP"},{"text":"B.Sc-B.Ed"},{"text":"BA-B.Ed"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Subject expertise"},{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Assessment design"},{"text":"Educational research"},{"text":"Digital learning"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 2 — Entry-Level Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible starting roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Teacher"},{"text":"Academic Content Associate"},{"text":"Curriculum Associate"},{"text":"Instructional Content Developer"},{"text":"Subject Matter Expert"},{"text":"Academic Coordinator"},{"text":"Learning Content Developer"},{"text":"Teaching Associate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 3 — Curriculum Development"},{"type":"p","text":"After gaining classroom/content experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Curriculum Developer"},{"text":"Instructional Designer"},{"text":"Academic Content Developer"},{"text":"Learning Experience Designer"},{"text":"Assessment Developer"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 4 — Leadership"},{"type":"p","text":"With substantial experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Curriculum Developer"},{"text":"Curriculum Lead"},{"text":"Academic Lead"},{"text":"Instructional Design Manager"},{"text":"Head of Curriculum"},{"text":"Academic Director"}]}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During ITEP / B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The exact curriculum varies by program, but students generally develop four major capabilities:"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Core Learning"],"rows":[[{"text":"Subject Knowledge"},{"text":"Mathematics, Science, Languages, Social Science or chosen discipline"}],[{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"How students learn and how subjects should be taught"}],[{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Child development, cognition, motivation and learning behaviour"}],[{"text":"Teaching Practice"},{"text":"Classroom observation, lesson planning and practicum"}],[{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Tests, rubrics, formative and summative assessment"}],[{"text":"Educational Technology"},{"text":"LMS, digital content, multimedia and online learning"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Educational research and evidence-based teaching"}],[{"text":"Curriculum"},{"text":"Curriculum design, sequencing and learning outcomes"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-Wise Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Education Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Child and adolescent development"},{"text":"Introduction to pedagogy"},{"text":"Communication skills"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Digital literacy"},{"text":"Subject foundations"},{"text":"Learning theories"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Build"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Teaching notes"},{"text":"Lesson plans"},{"text":"Reading summaries"},{"text":"Educational presentations"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Pedagogy & Instructional Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Subject-specific pedagogy"},{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Learning objectives"},{"text":"Teaching strategies"},{"text":"Classroom activities"},{"text":"Assessment basics"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Digital teaching"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to convert:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Curriculum Objective","Learning Outcome","Lesson Objective","Learning Activity","Assessment","Feedback","Learning Improvement"]},{"type":"p","text":"This design thinking becomes extremely important for curriculum development."}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Curriculum & Assessment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop deeper knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Curriculum frameworks"},{"text":"Curriculum sequencing"},{"text":"Learning outcomes"},{"text":"Competency-based education"},{"text":"Bloom's Taxonomy"},{"text":"Assessment design"},{"text":"Rubric development"},{"text":"Question-paper design"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"},{"text":"Inclusive curriculum"},{"text":"Educational technology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"A curriculum is not simply a collection of chapters."},{"type":"p","text":"A good curriculum connects:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Learning objectives","content","activities","assessments","competencies","outcomes"]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Practicum & Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final stage should focus heavily on practical experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complete curriculum units"},{"text":"Lesson sequences"},{"text":"Assessment frameworks"},{"text":"Teacher guides"},{"text":"Student workbooks"},{"text":"Digital learning modules"},{"text":"Project-based learning activities"},{"text":"Rubrics"},{"text":"Question banks"},{"text":"Complete teaching practicum and document what worked, what failed, and how the learning design could be improved."}]}]},{"heading":"Curriculum Development Framework","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Curriculum Developer should understand a systematic development cycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Identify Learner Needs","Define Competencies","Define Learning Outcomes","Select Content","Sequence Content","Design Learning Experiences","Create Learning Materials","Design Assessments","Pilot Curriculum","Collect Feedback","Analyze Learning Outcomes","Revise Curriculum","Deploy at Scale"]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Education"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Learning theories"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Curriculum"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Curriculum mapping"},{"text":"Curriculum alignment"},